{"id":"b7186d137addf271d4dd24c8d73c9985437baddc","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"b7186d137addf271d4dd24c8d73c9985437baddc","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/features/per_request_metrics.md","lines":["@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ When per-request metrics are enabled, the response includes a `metrics` object:","   },","   \"metrics\": {","     \"time_to_first_token_ms\": 85.2,","+    \"time_to_first_content_token_ms\": null,","     \"generation_time_ms\": 1240.5,","     \"queue_time_ms\": 12.3,","     \"mean_itl_ms\": 9.1,","@@ -49,6 +50,7 @@ When per-request metrics are enabled, the response includes a `metrics` object:"," | Field | Description |"," | --- | --- |"," | `time_to_first_token_ms` | Time from when the request was scheduled until the first output token was generated (TTFT). |","+| `time_to_first_content_token_ms` | Streaming only: time from request scheduling to the engine output batch that first produces non-empty text content, excluding reasoning and tool-call output. It equals `time_to_first_token_ms` when the first output batch produces text. Non-streaming requests return `null`; otherwise, the value is unset when no text content is produced. |"," | `generation_time_ms` | Decode time: time from the first output token to the last output token. Excludes both queue wait and prefill/TTFT. |"," | `queue_time_ms` | Time the request spent waiting in the scheduler queue before processing began. |"," | `mean_itl_ms` | Mean inter-token latency (average time between successive output tokens) during the decode phase. `null` for single-token responses. |","@@ -57,6 +59,37 @@ When per-request metrics are enabled, the response includes a `metrics` object:"," All fields are `null` if the underlying timing data is not available for that"," request."," ","+### Reasoning Models","+","+For streaming requests with a response parser, the first generated token may be","+reasoning output rather than text content. In that case,","+`time_to_first_content_token_ms` can be greater than","+`time_to_first_token_ms`.","+","+For example, start Qwen3 with its reasoning parser:","+","+```bash","+vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B \\","+  --reasoning-parser qwen3 \\","+  --enable-per-request-metrics","+```","+","+With `stream=True` and `stream_options={\"include_usage\": True}`, the final usage","+chunk's metrics may look like:","+","+```json","+{","+  \"metrics\": {","+    \"time_to_first_token_ms\": 108.2,","+    \"time_to_first_content_token_ms\": 268.2","+  }","+}","+```","+","+Here, the model began generating output after 108.2 ms, while text content","+started after 268.2 ms. This measures the first text content, not the final","+answer across a multi-turn tool workflow.","+"," !!! note","     Timing metrics describe a single generation stream, so they are only","     returned when the request maps to exactly one. They are suppressed (the","@@ -125,7 +158,8 @@ a single prompt's generation."," Per-request metrics are available on the `/v1/responses` endpoint using the"," common `metrics` object described above. Non-streaming responses include it at"," the top level. Streaming responses include it in the final response carried by","-the `response.completed` event; intermediate events do not include metrics.","+the `response.completed` or `response.incomplete` event; intermediate events do","+not include metrics."," "," Metrics are omitted for Responses requests that perform multiple"," model-generation turns, such as built-in tool-call workflows, because the"],"additions":35,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/event.rs","lines":["@@ -239,6 +239,8 @@ pub enum ChatEvent {","         usage: ChatTokenUsage,","         /// Engine lifecycle times used by frontend response metrics.","         timestamps: RequestTimestamps,","+        /// First engine output batch that produced non-empty parsed text.","+        first_content_token_ts: Option<f64>,","         /// Per-request speculative-decoding statistics emitted by the engine.",